Step 5: Temporary password relayed securely
Navigation: Phone / voice channel — not logged in CoreID
Read the temporary password to the caller verbally over the verified phone line. Never send it by email, chat, or ticket comment in plain text. See [CISA's guidance on requiring strong passwords](https://www.cisa.gov/secure-our-world/require-strong-passwords) for the reasoning behind credential-handling policy.
Step 6: Ticket resolved with audit note
Navigation: Ticketing system → ticket → Resolution notes
Log what was done (identity checks matched, temporary password issued, force-change enabled) and set the ticket to Resolved. This note is what satisfies the audit trail requirement — an admin-mediated reset with no note is a compliance gap.

